[14.006461, "o", "THREAT INTELLIGENCE ADVISORY — Struts Exfil campaign\r\n====================================================\r\n\r\nDistribution: TLP:AMBER   Analyst handoff   Confidence: HIGH   (IOCs are defanged)\r\nAffected host: struts-prod-01   Suspected origin IP: 198.51.100.167\r\n\r\n1. EXECUTIVE SUMMARY\r\nAn external actor executed a multi-stage post-compromise sequence. Endpoint alerting covered only part of it; several persistence and anti-forensic actions were silent. Map every on-disk finding to the ATT&CK techniques below and flag which are NOT in the SAS alert feed.\r\n\r\n2. ATT&CK TECHNIQUE MAPPING (MITRE ATT&CK Enterprise)\r\n   T1190      Exploit Public-Facing Application          [initial-access]  step 1: Struts2 OGNL RCE (CVE-2023-50164)\r\n   T1505.003  Web Shell                                  [persistence]  step 2: JSP webshell planted\r\n   T1059.004  Unix Shell                                 [execution]  step 3: shell execution\r\n   T1560.001  Archive via Utility                        [collection]  step 4: stage archive for exfil\r\n   T1048      Exfiltration Over Alternative Protocol     [exfiltration]  step 5: exfiltrate over HTTPS\r\n   T1098.004  SSH Authorized Keys                        [persistence]  step 6: authorized_keys backdoor\r\n   T1053.003  Cron                                       [execution]  step 7: cron persistence\r\n   T1070.002  Clear Linux or Mac System Logs             [defense-evasion]  step 8: selective auth-log wipe\r\n\r\n3. RELEVANT VULNERABILITIES (source: NVD, US-Gov public domain)\r\n   CVE-2023-50164  CVSS 9.8 (CRITICAL) v3.1  CWE=CWE-552\r\n      An attacker can manipulate file upload params to enable paths traversal and under some circumstances this can lead to uploading a malicious file which can be used to perform Remote Code Execution.\r\nUsers are recommended to upgrade to version\r\n      ref: http://packetstormsecurity.com/files/176157/Struts-S2-066-File-Upload-Remote-Code-Execution.html\r\n\r\n4. INDICATORS OF COMPROMISE (defanged)\r\n   ip     198.51.100.167\r\n   c2     update-struts[.]example[.]cn\r\n   pool   stratum+tcp[:]//xmr[.]struts[.]evil[:]3333\r\n   wallet 4A000000000000000000e40b218944d0\r\n\r\nAttribution: MITRE ATT&CK(R) (C) The MITRE Corporation, CC BY 4.0. CVE/CVSS from the U.S. National Vulnerability Database (public domain).\r\n\u001b[?2004hroot@e62f4246bce8:/app# "]
