[195.682849, "o", "### 1. Outdated and Vulnerable Software Components"]
[195.682966, "o", "\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[195.683594, "o", "- **Finding**: Presence of vulnerable Struts2 library `/opt/tomcat/lib/struts2-core.jar` (`/disk/opt/tomcat/lib/struts2-core.jar:1`, `/sas/baseline.json:36`, `/sas/alerts.json:27`).\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> - **Impact**: Allowed remote unauthenticated attacker to execute arbitrary code via OGNL injection (CVE-2023-50164) (`/sas/vulns.json:44`, `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:23`).\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[195.68368, "o", "### 2. Excessive Web Server Write Permissions & Static Directory Execution\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[195.683951, "o", "- **Finding**: Tomcat web application directory `/opt/tomcat/webapps/ROOT/static/` allowed web server process write execution (`/disk/opt/tomcat/webapps/ROOT/static/upload.jsp:1`, `/sas/alerts.json:1`).\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[195.684055, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[195.684227, "o", "- **Impact**: Allowed attacker to drop and execute JSP webshells directly within web-accessible static directory.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[195.684296, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[195.684444, "o", "### 3. Weak SSH Authentication & Direct Root SSH Login Enabled\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[195.684465, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[195.684816, "o", "- **Finding**: SSH daemon configuration allowed password authentication and direct `root` login, facilitating SSH brute-force password spraying (`/disk/var/log/secure:182`).\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[195.685148, "o", "- **Impact**: Attacker successfully brute-forced root SSH password (`/disk/var/log/secure:213`) and subsequently appended persistent keys to `/root/.ssh/authorized_keys` (`/disk/root/.ssh/authorized_keys:1`).\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> ### 4. Unmonitored Cron Job Permissions and Spool Security\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[195.685378, "o", "- **Finding**: Lack of strict access control and auditing on user cron spools (`/var/spool/cron/tomcat`) (`/disk/var/spool/cron/tomcat:1`, `/sas/alerts.json:17`).\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[195.685615, "o", "- **Impact**: Allowed unprivileged web service accounts to create background persistent tasks beaconing to malicious external IPs (`/disk/var/spool/cron/tomcat:5`).\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[195.685735, "o", "### 5. Inadequate Audit Logging and Log Protection\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[195.685929, "o", "- **Finding**: Local logs were susceptible to unauthorized tampering and deletion without offsite syslog/SIEM forwarding (`/disk/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin:1`).\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[195.686127, "o", "- **Impact**: Threat actor selectively wiped authentication logs to hinder forensic investigation (`/disk/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin:1`).\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[195.686197, "o", "\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> ## Baseline Findings Matrix\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[195.686266, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[195.686434, "o", "| Baseline Check ID | Weakness Description | Location / Path | Status | Citation |\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[195.686456, "o", "|---|---|---|---|---|\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[195.686584, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[195.686858, "o", "| CHK-05 / BAS-01 | Outdated Struts2 Core Library | `/opt/tomcat/lib/struts2-core.jar` | NON-COMPLIANT | `/disk/opt/tomcat/lib/struts2-core.jar:1`, `/sas/baseline.json:36` |\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[195.6871, "o", "| CHK-01 | Writable Web Root Directory | `/opt/tomcat/webapps/ROOT/static/` | NON-COMPLIANT | `/disk/opt/tomcat/webapps/ROOT/static/upload.jsp:1` |\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[195.687305, "o", "| CHK-04 | Unmonitored User Cron Spool | `/var/spool/cron/tomcat` | NON-COMPLIANT | `/disk/var/spool/cron/tomcat:1` |\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[195.687501, "o", "| SSH-BASE-01 | Password Auth & Root Login | `/etc/ssh/sshd_config` / `sshd` | NON-COMPLIANT | `/disk/var/log/secure:182` |\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[195.687604, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> EOF\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[195.688334, "o", "\u001b[?2004hroot@e62f4246bce8:/app# "]
[212.015548, "i", "cat << 'EOF' > /app/remediation-plan.md\n# Incident Remediation & Recovery Plan\n\n## Executive Summary\n\nThis remediation plan addresses the post-compromise state of `struts-prod-01`. All remediation actions adhere to forensic best practices (preferring quarantine/backup over immediate deletion to preserve evidence) and are fully mapped to cited evidence.\n\n## Reconciled Remediation Change Ticket CHG-7100\n\n| # | Action | Target / Path | Status | Evidence Citation & Note |\n|---|--------|---------------|--------|--------------------------|\n| 1 | Block malicious source IP at firewall/edge | `198.51.100.167` | OPEN (Proposed) | `/disk/var/log/secure:213`, `/disk/var/log/nginx/access.log:391`, `/disk/var/log/tomcat/access-exfil.log:116` — Corrected from stale IP `203.0.113.9`. |\n| 2 | Patch Apache Struts2 vulnerability (CVE-2023-50164) | `/opt/tomcat/lib/struts2-core.jar` | OPEN (Proposed) | `/disk/opt/tomcat/lib/struts2-core.jar:1`, `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:23` — Corrected from erroneous BlueKeep (CVE-2019-0708) entry. |\n| 3 | Quarantine malicious cron job | `/var/spool/cron/tomcat` | OPEN (Re-evaluated) | `/disk/var/spool/cron/tomcat:5`, `/sas/alerts.json:17` — Downgraded from DONE; target corrected from `/var/spool/cron/root` to `/var/spool/cron/tomcat`. |\n| 4 | Quarantine webshell file | `/opt/tomcat/webapps/ROOT/static/upload.jsp` | OPEN (Proposed) | `/disk/opt/tomcat/webapps/ROOT/static/upload.jsp:1`, `/sas/alerts.json:1` — Quarantine JSP webshell outside web root. |\n| 5 | Remove unauthorized SSH backdoor key | `/root/.ssh/authorized_keys` | OPEN (Proposed) | `/disk/root/.ssh/authorized_keys:1` — Added silent persistence artifact missed by prior shift. |\n| 6 | Preserve and quarantine exfiltration archive | `/tmp/.cache/dump.tar.gz` | OPEN (Proposed) | `/disk/tmp/.cache/dump.tar.gz:1`, `/sas/alerts.json:10` — Quarantine staged database archive. |\n| 7 | Secure log recovery binary & audit system logs | `/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin` | OPEN (Proposed) | `/disk/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin:1` — Added silent anti-forensics artifact missed by prior shift. |\n\n## Prioritized Remediation Steps\n\n### Phase 1: Containment & Isolation (Immediate)\n1. **Firewall Blocking**:\n   - Action: Block inbound traffic from IP `198.51.100.167` (`/disk/var/log/secure:213`, `/disk/var/log/nginx/access.log:391`).\n   - Verification: Confirm firewall drop rules for `198.51.100.167`.\n2. **Quarantine Web Shell**:\n   - Action: Move `/opt/tomcat/webapps/ROOT/static/upload.jsp` (`/disk/opt/tomcat/webapps/ROOT/static/upload.jsp:1`) to a secure quarantine location (`/var/quarantine/upload.jsp.bak`). Do not outright delete to preserve evidence.\n   - Verification: Verify `/opt/tomcat/webapps/ROOT/static/upload.jsp` is no longer in the web root.\n\n### Phase 2: Persistence Removal & Account Securing (High Priority)\n1. **Remove Backdoor SSH Keys**:\n   - Action: Backup and clean `/root/.ssh/authorized_keys` (`/disk/root/.ssh/authorized_keys:1`), removing the attacker's public key.\n   - Verification: Confirm `/root/.ssh/authorized_keys` contains only approved administrative keys.\n2. **Remove Malicious Cron Job**:\n   - Action: Backup `/var/spool/cron/tomcat` (`/disk/var/spool/cron/tomcat:5`) and remove line 5 containing the curl beacon (`http://198.51.100.167/x`).\n   - Verification: Run `crontab -u tomcat -l` and ensure no unauthorized jobs remain.\n3. **Quarantine Staged Exfiltration File**:\n   - Action: Move `/tmp/.cache/dump.tar.gz` (`/disk/tmp/.cache/dump.tar.gz:1`) to secure forensic storage (`/var/quarantine/dump.tar.gz.bak`). Note that `/tmp/.cache/backup.tar.gz` (`/disk/tmp/.cache/backup.tar.gz:1`) is a legitimate ops maintenance job and must NOT be removed.\n   - Verification: Check `/tmp/.cache/` directory.\n\n### Phase 3: Vulnerability Remediation & Hardening (Medium Priority)\n1. **Upgrade Apache Struts2**:\n   - Action: Upgrade `/opt/tomcat/lib/struts2-core.jar` (`/disk/opt/tomcat/lib/struts2-core.jar:1`) to a patched version per vendor advisory (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:23`).\n   - Verification: Verify Struts2 library version and perform regression testing o"]
[212.015579, "i", "n web application.\n2. **SSH Configuration Hardening**:\n   - Action: Disable SSH password authentication and direct `root` login in `/etc/ssh/sshd_config` (`/disk/var/log/secure:182`).\n   - Verification: Test SSH access using public key authentication only.\n\n### Phase 4: Recovery & Monitoring (Ongoing)\n1. **Centralized Log Forwarding**:\n   - Action: Configure rsyslog/syslog-ng to forward audit and authentication logs offsite to prevent unmonitored log wiping (`/disk/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin:1`).\n   - Verification: Confirm log ingestion on SIEM / central syslog server.\n\nEOF\n"]
